# Known vulnerabilities that scripts/vulncheck.sh tolerates.
#
# The scan fails on every finding that is not listed here, and it also fails
# when an entry here is no longer reported (so stale exceptions get removed).
# Each entry needs a reason and a condition for removing it.
#
# Format: <ID> <date reviewed> <reason>

# gRPC server panic on a request with a missing :authority/Host header.
# Affects the peer listener (the only gRPC server in this project).
#   - Latest stable grpc-go is v1.84.0, which is affected. The fix exists only
#     on an unreleased development branch (v1.85.0-dev pseudo-version), and
#     this project pins released versions only.
#   - Impact here is availability, not safety: a panic stops one node, which
#     is a crash failure the cluster is built to tolerate, and the node
#     recovers its state on restart.
#   - In secure mode the peer listener requires a client certificate signed by
#     the cluster CA before any HTTP/2 request is read, so only a holder of a
#     peer certificate can send the request. In --insecure-dev mode anyone who
#     can reach the peer port can; that mode is documented as local-only.
# Remove when: grpc-go v1.85.0 is released; upgrade and delete this entry.
GO-2026-6443 2026-10-02 no released grpc-go contains the fix; availability-only; peer port requires mTLS in secure mode
